{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789825246004,"sessionID":"ses_f461fa331ffe0Vx8rAYcMiXg6i","part":{"partID":"prt_0b9e5e1f30017KDLUGil66BV0i","sessionID":"ses_f461fa331ffe0Vx8rAYcMiXg6i","messageID":"msg_0b9e5da7c001NktJBYIwZDGwZ1","type":"tool","id":"call_00_iMmdVFP0UkMmGSG5iBje4106","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/tmp/opencode/work/filing_pages.txt","offset":4742,"limit":60},"output":"Read file /tmp/opencode/work/filing_pages.txt, lines 4742-4801\n4742:  Financing of the Merger \n4743: \n4744:  The merger agreement does not contain any condition to the obligations of the Buyer Entities or Merger Subsidiary relating to the\n4745: receipt of financing by the Buyer Entities. Parent has made available \n4746: \n4747: 58\n4748: \n4749:  ZEQ.=5,SEQ=64,EFW=\"2217482\",CP=\"MAC-GRAY CORPORATION\",DN=\"1\",CHK=85691,FOLIO='58',FILE='DISK112:[13ZCX1.13ZCX46801]DM46801A.;10',USER='HYUNG',CD=';2-DEC-2013;13:16' \n4750: \n4751: [[page 59]]\n4752: \n4753: Table of Contents\n4754: \n4755: for\n4756: purposes of funding the merger consideration an aggregate of $594 million of capital (the Pamplona commitment amount), which is committed pursuant to the Pamplona commitment letter\n4757: delivered to the Buyer Entities by Pamplona Capital Partners III, L.P. dated as of October 14, 2013. \n4758: \n4759:  The\n4760: commitment amount will be used by the Buyer Entities to fund the merger consideration at closing (including as a result of a judgment of specific performance) and any other payments\n4761: to be made by the Buyer Entities or Mac-Gray at closing, and all associated costs and expenses of the merger for which the Buyer Entities are responsible, which we refer to as the closing funding\n4762: obligations. In addition, Pamplona and the Buyer Entities will be jointly and severally liable for any amounts that may be owed by the Buyer Entities with respect to any breach of the merger\n4763: agreement, including the Parent Termination Fee or any payment of monetary damages awarded to Mac-Gray, provided that Pamplona's liability for such damages will not exceed $50 million, which we\n4764: refer to as the damages\n4765: amount (provided further that the liability of Buyer Entities shall be unlimited). Mac-Gray is an express third party beneficiary of the Pamplona commitment letter. \n4766: \n4767:  The\n4768: obligation of Pamplona to fund the closing funding obligations is conditioned upon (a) all conditions to the obligations of Parent and Merger Subsidiary set forth in the\n4769: merger agreement having been satisfied or waived as of the date of the closing pursuant to the terms of the merger agreement (other than those conditions that by their nature cannot be satisfied until\n4770: the closing and that would be satisfied assuming the Closing would occur); or (b) Mac-Gray obtaining, as contemplated in the merger agreement, an award of specific performance by a court of\n4771: competent jurisdiction in a final non-appealable judgment requiring Parent to effect the closing, or other equitable remedy to specifically enforce the obligations of Parent and Merger Subsidiary to\n4772: effect the closing on the terms set forth in the merger agreement. \n4773: \n4774:  The\n4775: obligation of Pamplona to pay all or any portion of the damages amount is conditioned upon any of the following having occurred: (a) following termination of the merger\n4776: agreement (other than a termination upon which the Parent termination fee is due, which is summarized in clause (b) of this paragraph), Mac-Gray's having obtained in an award by a court of\n4777: competent jurisdiction in a final non-appealable judgment monetary damages against Parent or Merger Subsidiary as permitted by the terms of the merger agreement or (b) the termination of the\n4778: merger agreement such that the Parent termination fee and any related amounts become payable to Mac-Gray (provided, in such case, Pamplona will not be required to fund or pay any amounts in excess of\n4779: the Parent termination fee plus any other amounts due and payable to Mac-Gray pursuant to the merger agreement). The amount payable by Pamplona pursuant to the foregoing sentence will be reduced\n4780: dollar for dollar by the amount actually paid to Mac-Gray by any Buyer Entity or Merger Subsidiary in satisfaction thereof. \n4781: \n4782:  Subject\n4783: to the exception at the end of this sentence, Mac-Gray's remedies against Pamplona with respect to the Pamplona commitment amount and the obligations summarized above are the\n4784: exclusive remedies available to Mac-Gray and its affiliates against Pamplona in respect of any liabilities or obligations arising under, or in connection with, the merger agreement or the transactions\n4785: contemplated thereby, or in respect of any oral representations made in connection therewith, including in the event Parent or Merger Subsidiary breaches its obligations under the merger agreement,\n4786: whether or not any such breach is caused by Pamplona's breach of its obligations under the Pamplona commitment letter, except for the right of Mac-Gray to enforce its rights thereunder in accordance\n4787: with the terms thereof, including, without limitation, specifically enforcing the provisions of the Pamplona commitment letter to cause Pamplona to fund the Pamplona commitment amount to permit the\n4788: closing of the merger to occur subject to and in accordance with the terms and conditions of the merger agreement and the Pamplona commitment letter. \n4789: \n4790:  Delisting and Deregistration of Mac-Gray Common Stock \n4791: \n4792:  If the merger is completed, Mac-Gray common stock will be removed from listing on the New York Stock Exchange and deregistered under\n4793: the Exchange Act and we will no longer file periodic reports with the SEC. \n4794: \n4795: 59\n4796: \n4797:  ZEQ.=6,SEQ=65,EFW=\"2217482\",CP=\"MAC-GRAY CORPORATION\",DN=\"1\",CHK=1032666,FOLIO='59',FILE='DISK112:[13ZCX1.13ZCX46801]DM46801A.;10',USER='HYUNG',CD=';2-DEC-2013;13:16' \n4798: \n4799: [[page 60]]\n4800:  THIS IS THE END OF A COMPOSITION COMPONENT \n4801: \n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 4802]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /tmp/opencode/work/filing_pages.txt, lines 4742-4801\n4742:  Financing of the Merger \n4743: \n4744:  The merger agreement does not contain any condition to the obligations of the Buyer Entities or Merger Subsidiary relating to the\n4745: receipt of financing by the Buyer Entities. Parent has made available \n4746: \n4747: 58\n4748: \n4749:  ZEQ.=5,SEQ=64,EFW=\"2217482\",CP=\"MAC-GRAY CORPORATION\",DN=\"1\",CHK=85691,FOLIO='58',FILE='DISK112:[13ZCX1.13ZCX46801]DM46801A.;10',USER='HYUNG',CD=';2-DEC-2013;13:16' \n4750: \n4751: [[page 59]]\n4752: \n4753: Table of Contents\n4754: \n4755: for\n4756: purposes of funding the merger consideration an aggregate of $594 million of capital (the Pamplona commitment amount), which is committed pursuant to the Pamplona commitment letter\n4757: delivered to the Buyer Entities by Pamplona Capital Partners III, L.P. dated as of October 14, 2013. \n4758: \n4759:  The\n4760: commitment amount will be used by the Buyer Entities to fund the merger consideration at closing (including as a result of a judgment of specific performance) and any other payments\n4761: to be made by the Buyer Entities or Mac-Gray at closing, and all associated costs and expenses of the merger for which the Buyer Entities are responsible, which we refer to as the closing funding\n4762: obligations. In addition, Pamplona and the Buyer Entities will be jointly and severally liable for any amounts that may be owed by the Buyer Entities with respect to any breach of the merger\n4763: agreement, including the Parent Termination Fee or any payment of monetary damages awarded to Mac-Gray, provided that Pamplona's liability for such damages will not exceed $50 million, which we\n4764: refer to as the damages\n4765: amount (provided further that the liability of Buyer Entities shall be unlimited). Mac-Gray is an express third party beneficiary of the Pamplona commitment letter. \n4766: \n4767:  The\n4768: obligation of Pamplona to fund the closing funding obligations is conditioned upon (a) all conditions to the obligations of Parent and Merger Subsidiary set forth in the\n4769: merger agreement having been satisfied or waived as of the date of the closing pursuant to the terms of the merger agreement (other than those conditions that by their nature cannot be satisfied until\n4770: the closing and that would be satisfied assuming the Closing would occur); or (b) Mac-Gray obtaining, as contemplated in the merger agreement, an award of specific performance by a court of\n4771: competent jurisdiction in a final non-appealable judgment requiring Parent to effect the closing, or other equitable remedy to specifically enforce the obligations of Parent and Merger Subsidiary to\n4772: effect the closing on the terms set forth in the merger agreement. \n4773: \n4774:  The\n4775: obligation of Pamplona to pay all or any portion of the damages amount is conditioned upon any of the following having occurred: (a) following termination of the merger\n4776: agreement (other than a termination upon which the Parent termination fee is due, which is summarized in clause (b) of this paragraph), Mac-Gray's having obtained in an award by a court of\n4777: competent jurisdiction in a final non-appealable judgment monetary damages against Parent or Merger Subsidiary as permitted by the terms of the merger agreement or (b) the termination of the\n4778: merger agreement such that the Parent termination fee and any related amounts become payable to Mac-Gray (provided, in such case, Pamplona will not be required to fund or pay any amounts in excess of\n4779: the Parent termination fee plus any other amounts due and payable to Mac-Gray pursuant to the merger agreement). The amount payable by Pamplona pursuant to the foregoing sentence will be reduced\n4780: dollar for dollar by the amount actually paid to Mac-Gray by any Buyer Entity or Merger Subsidiary in satisfaction thereof. \n4781: \n4782:  Subject\n4783: to the exception at the end of this sentence, Mac-Gray's remedies against Pamplona with respect to the Pamplona commitment amount and the obligations summarized above are the\n4784: exclusive remedies available to Mac-Gray and its affiliates against Pamplona in respect of any liabilities or obligations arising under, or in connection with, the merger agreement or the transactions\n4785: contemplated thereby, or in respect of any oral representations made in connection therewith, including in the event Parent or Merger Subsidiary breaches its obligations under the merger agreement,\n4786: whether or not any such breach is caused by Pamplona's breach of its obligations under the Pamplona commitment letter, except for the right of Mac-Gray to enforce its rights thereunder in accordance\n4787: with the terms thereof, including, without limitation, specifically enforcing the provisions of the Pamplona commitment letter to cause Pamplona to fund the Pamplona commitment amount to permit the\n4788: closing of the merger to occur subject to and in accordance with the terms and conditions of the merger agreement and the Pamplona commitment letter. \n4789: \n4790:  Delisting and Deregistration of Mac-Gray Common Stock \n4791: \n4792:  If the merger is completed, Mac-Gray common stock will be removed from listing on the New York Stock Exchange and deregistered under\n4793: the Exchange Act and we will no longer file periodic reports with the SEC. \n4794: \n4795: 59\n4796: \n4797:  ZEQ.=6,SEQ=65,EFW=\"2217482\",CP=\"MAC-GRAY CORPORATION\",DN=\"1\",CHK=1032666,FOLIO='59',FILE='DISK112:[13ZCX1.13ZCX46801]DM46801A.;10',USER='HYUNG',CD=';2-DEC-2013;13:16' \n4798: \n4799: [[page 60]]\n4800:  THIS IS THE END OF A COMPOSITION COMPONENT \n4801: \n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 4802]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"/tmp/opencode/work/filing_pages.txt\", \"offset\": 4742, \"limit\": 60}"},"time":{"start":1789825245683,"end":1789825246004}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789825246011,"sessionID":"ses_f461fa331ffe0Vx8rAYcMiXg6i","part":{"partID":"prt_0b9e5e276001p6z0CuVCMHyJ6q","sessionID":"ses_f461fa331ffe0Vx8rAYcMiXg6i","messageID":"msg_0b9e5da7c001NktJBYIwZDGwZ1","type":"tool","id":"call_01_C3ywSYXxICGPvATbjB0X7294","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/tmp/opencode/work/filing_pages.txt","offset":920,"limit":60},"output":"Read file /tmp/opencode/work/filing_pages.txt, lines 920-979\n920: are advisable and in the best interests of Mac-Gray and its stockholders, (2) approved the merger agreement and (3) recommends that Mac-Gray stockholders adopt the merger agreement. Accordingly, the Mac-Gray Board of\n921: Directors unanimously recommends that holders of Mac-Gray common stock vote \"FOR\" the proposal to adopt the merger agreement at the special\n922: meeting. The Mac-Gray Board of Directors also unanimously recommends that holders of Mac-Gray common stock vote \"FOR\" the proposal to approve, on an\n923: advisory (non-binding) basis, the \"golden parachute\" compensation payable or that could become payable to the named executive officers of Mac-Gray in connection with the merger pursuant to the terms\n924: of the merger agreement and pre-existing severance arrangements and \"FOR\" the adjournment proposal.\n925: \n926: 5\n927: \n928:  ZEQ.=5,SEQ=11,EFW=\"2217482\",CP=\"MAC-GRAY CORPORATION\",DN=\"1\",CHK=676964,FOLIO='5',FILE='DISK112:[13ZCX1.13ZCX46801]DA46801A.;18',USER='HYUNG',CD=';2-DEC-2013;13:15' \n929: \n930: [[page 6]]\n931: \n932: Table of Contents\n933: \n934:  For\n935: the factors considered by our Board of Directors in reaching its decision to approve the merger agreement, see \"The Merger—Reasons for the Merger and Recommendation of\n936: our Board of Directors\" beginning on page 42 of this proxy statement. \n937: \n938:  Opinion of Mac-Gray's Financial Advisor (Page 45 and Annex B) \n939: \n940:  In connection with the merger, Merrill Lynch, Pierce, Fenner & Smith Incorporated, which we refer to as BofA Merrill Lynch,\n941: Mac-Gray's financial advisor, delivered to the Special Committee a written opinion, dated October 14, 2013, as to the fairness, from a financial point of view and as of the date of the opinion,\n942: of the consideration to be received by holders of Mac-Gray common stock in the merger, which we refer to as the merger consideration. The full text of the written opinion, dated October 14,\n943: 2013, of BofA Merrill Lynch, which describes, among other things, the assumptions made, procedures followed, factors considered and limitations on the review undertaken, is attached as Annex B\n944: to this proxy statement and is incorporated by reference herein in\n945: its entirety. BofA Merrill Lynch provided its opinion to the Special Committee (in its capacity as such) for the benefit and use of the Special Committee in connection with and\n946: for purposes of its evaluation of the merger consideration from a financial point of view. BofA Merrill Lynch's opinion does not address any other aspect of the merger and no opinion or view was\n947: expressed as to the relative merits of the merger in comparison to other strategies or transactions that might be available to Mac-Gray or in which Mac-Gray might engage or as to the underlying\n948: business decision of Mac-Gray to proceed with or effect the merger. BofA Merrill Lynch's opinion does not address any other aspect of the merger and does not constitute a recommendation to any\n949: stockholder as to how to vote or act in connection with the merger or any related matter.\n950: \n951:  Financing of the Merger (Page 58) \n952: \n953:  The merger agreement does not contain any condition to the obligations of the Buyer Entities or Merger Subsidiary relating to the\n954: receipt of financing by the Buyer Entities. Parent will fund the merger consideration from an aggregate of $594 million of capital, which we refer to as the Pamplona commitment amount and which\n955: is committed pursuant to a commitment letter delivered to the Buyer Entities by Pamplona Capital Partners III, L.P. dated as of October 14, 2013, which we refer to as the Pamplona\n956: commitment letter. \n957: \n958:  The\n959: Pamplona commitment amount will be used by the Buyer Entities to fund the merger consideration at closing (including as a result of a final non-appealable judgment of specific\n960: performance) and any other payments to be made by the Buyer Entities or Mac-Gray at closing, and all associated costs and expenses of the merger for which the Buyer Entities are responsible. In\n961: addition, Pamplona and the Buyer Entities will be jointly and severally liable for any amounts that may be owed by the Buyer Entities with respect to any breach of the merger agreement, including the\n962: Parent Termination Fee or any payment of monetary damages awarded to Mac-Gray, provided that Pamplona's liability for such damages will not exceed $50 million (provided further, that the\n963: liability of Buyer Entities for such damages shall be unlimited). Mac-Gray is an express third party beneficiary of the Pamplona commitment letter. \n964: \n965:  Conditions to the Merger (Page 77) \n966: \n967:  The obligations of Parent and Merger Subsidiary, on the one hand, and Mac-Gray, on the other hand, to consummate the merger are subject\n968: to the satisfaction at or prior to the closing of the merger of the following conditions:\n969: \n970: •adoption of the merger agreement by an affirmative vote of the holders of a majority of the outstanding shares of Mac-Gray\n971: common stock; \n972: \n973: 6\n974: \n975:  ZEQ.=6,SEQ=12,EFW=\"2217482\",CP=\"MAC-GRAY CORPORATION\",DN=\"1\",CHK=222593,FOLIO='6',FILE='DISK112:[13ZCX1.13ZCX46801]DA46801A.;18',USER='HYUNG',CD=';2-DEC-2013;13:15' \n976: \n977: [[page 7]]\n978: \n979: Table of Contents\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 980]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /tmp/opencode/work/filing_pages.txt, lines 920-979\n920: are advisable and in the best interests of Mac-Gray and its stockholders, (2) approved the merger agreement and (3) recommends that Mac-Gray stockholders adopt the merger agreement. Accordingly, the Mac-Gray Board of\n921: Directors unanimously recommends that holders of Mac-Gray common stock vote \"FOR\" the proposal to adopt the merger agreement at the special\n922: meeting. The Mac-Gray Board of Directors also unanimously recommends that holders of Mac-Gray common stock vote \"FOR\" the proposal to approve, on an\n923: advisory (non-binding) basis, the \"golden parachute\" compensation payable or that could become payable to the named executive officers of Mac-Gray in connection with the merger pursuant to the terms\n924: of the merger agreement and pre-existing severance arrangements and \"FOR\" the adjournment proposal.\n925: \n926: 5\n927: \n928:  ZEQ.=5,SEQ=11,EFW=\"2217482\",CP=\"MAC-GRAY CORPORATION\",DN=\"1\",CHK=676964,FOLIO='5',FILE='DISK112:[13ZCX1.13ZCX46801]DA46801A.;18',USER='HYUNG',CD=';2-DEC-2013;13:15' \n929: \n930: [[page 6]]\n931: \n932: Table of Contents\n933: \n934:  For\n935: the factors considered by our Board of Directors in reaching its decision to approve the merger agreement, see \"The Merger—Reasons for the Merger and Recommendation of\n936: our Board of Directors\" beginning on page 42 of this proxy statement. \n937: \n938:  Opinion of Mac-Gray's Financial Advisor (Page 45 and Annex B) \n939: \n940:  In connection with the merger, Merrill Lynch, Pierce, Fenner & Smith Incorporated, which we refer to as BofA Merrill Lynch,\n941: Mac-Gray's financial advisor, delivered to the Special Committee a written opinion, dated October 14, 2013, as to the fairness, from a financial point of view and as of the date of the opinion,\n942: of the consideration to be received by holders of Mac-Gray common stock in the merger, which we refer to as the merger consideration. The full text of the written opinion, dated October 14,\n943: 2013, of BofA Merrill Lynch, which describes, among other things, the assumptions made, procedures followed, factors considered and limitations on the review undertaken, is attached as Annex B\n944: to this proxy statement and is incorporated by reference herein in\n945: its entirety. BofA Merrill Lynch provided its opinion to the Special Committee (in its capacity as such) for the benefit and use of the Special Committee in connection with and\n946: for purposes of its evaluation of the merger consideration from a financial point of view. BofA Merrill Lynch's opinion does not address any other aspect of the merger and no opinion or view was\n947: expressed as to the relative merits of the merger in comparison to other strategies or transactions that might be available to Mac-Gray or in which Mac-Gray might engage or as to the underlying\n948: business decision of Mac-Gray to proceed with or effect the merger. BofA Merrill Lynch's opinion does not address any other aspect of the merger and does not constitute a recommendation to any\n949: stockholder as to how to vote or act in connection with the merger or any related matter.\n950: \n951:  Financing of the Merger (Page 58) \n952: \n953:  The merger agreement does not contain any condition to the obligations of the Buyer Entities or Merger Subsidiary relating to the\n954: receipt of financing by the Buyer Entities. Parent will fund the merger consideration from an aggregate of $594 million of capital, which we refer to as the Pamplona commitment amount and which\n955: is committed pursuant to a commitment letter delivered to the Buyer Entities by Pamplona Capital Partners III, L.P. dated as of October 14, 2013, which we refer to as the Pamplona\n956: commitment letter. \n957: \n958:  The\n959: Pamplona commitment amount will be used by the Buyer Entities to fund the merger consideration at closing (including as a result of a final non-appealable judgment of specific\n960: performance) and any other payments to be made by the Buyer Entities or Mac-Gray at closing, and all associated costs and expenses of the merger for which the Buyer Entities are responsible. In\n961: addition, Pamplona and the Buyer Entities will be jointly and severally liable for any amounts that may be owed by the Buyer Entities with respect to any breach of the merger agreement, including the\n962: Parent Termination Fee or any payment of monetary damages awarded to Mac-Gray, provided that Pamplona's liability for such damages will not exceed $50 million (provided further, that the\n963: liability of Buyer Entities for such damages shall be unlimited). Mac-Gray is an express third party beneficiary of the Pamplona commitment letter. \n964: \n965:  Conditions to the Merger (Page 77) \n966: \n967:  The obligations of Parent and Merger Subsidiary, on the one hand, and Mac-Gray, on the other hand, to consummate the merger are subject\n968: to the satisfaction at or prior to the closing of the merger of the following conditions:\n969: \n970: •adoption of the merger agreement by an affirmative vote of the holders of a majority of the outstanding shares of Mac-Gray\n971: common stock; \n972: \n973: 6\n974: \n975:  ZEQ.=6,SEQ=12,EFW=\"2217482\",CP=\"MAC-GRAY CORPORATION\",DN=\"1\",CHK=222593,FOLIO='6',FILE='DISK112:[13ZCX1.13ZCX46801]DA46801A.;18',USER='HYUNG',CD=';2-DEC-2013;13:15' \n976: \n977: [[page 7]]\n978: \n979: Table of Contents\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 980]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"/tmp/opencode/work/filing_pages.txt\", \"offset\": 920, \"limit\": 60}"},"time":{"start":1789825245814,"end":1789825246011}}}}
