{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789825403059,"sessionID":"ses_f461fa331ffe0Vx8rAYcMiXg6i","part":{"partID":"prt_0b9e82af2001LFzs17e8ZdP1Lx","sessionID":"ses_f461fa331ffe0Vx8rAYcMiXg6i","messageID":"msg_0b9e75c6a001QFWYPldIMriPa1","type":"tool","id":"call_00_DHZExxJmGyZgLZgmePba5324","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/opencode/work && python3 - <<'PYEOF'\nimport re\n\ntext = open('filing_pages.txt').read()\n\n# Build page index: position -> page label, using markers\nmarkers = [(m.start(), m.group(1)) for m in re.finditer(r\"\\[\\[page (\\S+)\\]\\]\", text)]\ndef page_at(pos):\n    lab = None\n    for p, l in markers:\n        if p <= pos:\n            lab = l\n        else:\n            break\n    return lab\n\n# normalized text for searching\nnorm = re.sub(r'\\s+', ' ', text)\n# map normalized positions back approx: do search on norm, then find page by nearest original index\ndef find_page(quote):\n    q = re.sub(r'\\s+', ' ', quote).strip()\n    idx = norm.find(q)\n    if idx < 0:\n        return None, None\n    # map norm index to original index: count words\n    # simpler: find the first 40 chars of q in original text (whitespace-insensitive walk)\n    # walk: build mapping norm char -> orig char\n    return idx, q\n\n# build mapping from norm index to original index\nmapping = []\ni = 0\nn = 0\nwhile i < len(text):\n    c = text[i]\n    if c.isspace():\n        # collapse\n        while i < len(text) and text[i].isspace():\n            i += 1\n        norm = norm  # noop\n        mapping.append(len(mapping))\n        n += 1\n    else:\n        mapping.append(n)\n        n += 1\n        i += 1\n# Hmm this mapping approach is getting complicated; simpler: rebuild norm with index list.\nPYEOF\necho \"---- now the real approach ----\"\npython3 - <<'PYEOF'\nimport re\ntext = open('/tmp/opencode/work/filing_pages.txt').read()\nmarkers = [(m.start(), m.group(1)) for m in re.finditer(r\"\\[\\[page (\\S+)\\]\\]\", text)]\n\n# Build normalized string with per-character original index\nout = []\norig_idx = []\ni = 0\nprev_space = True\nwhile i < len(text):\n    if text[i].isspace():\n        if not prev_space:\n            out.append(' ')\n            orig_idx.append(i)\n        prev_space = True\n        i += 1\n    else:\n        out.append(text[i])\n        orig_idx.append(i)\n        prev_space = False\n        i += 1\nnorm = ''.join(out)\n\ndef page_for_pos(pos):\n    lab = None\n    for p, l in markers:\n        if p <= pos:\n            lab = l\n        else:\n            break\n    return lab\n\ndef find(quote):\n    q = re.sub(r'\\s+', ' ', quote).strip()\n    idx = norm.find(q)\n    if idx < 0:\n        return None, []\n    pages = []\n    # pages spanned\n    last = None\n    for j in range(idx, idx+len(q)):\n        p = page_for_pos(orig_idx[j])\n        if p != last:\n            pages.append(p)\n            last = p\n    return idx, pages\n\nquotes = {\n\"1\":\"In connection with Mac-Gray's consideration of a possible acquisition of CSC, which we refer to as the 2011-2012 Discussions, Mac-Gray engaged BofA Merrill Lynch on October 23, 2012\",\n\"2\":\"representatives of BofA Merrill Lynch, as instructed by the Board, telephoned a representative of Party A to discuss generally a possible business combination between Party A and Mac-Gray\",\n\"3\":\"Goodwin Procter LLP, outside legal counsel to Mac-Gray, were also in attendance for all or portions of the meeting\",\n\"4\":\"On May 15, 2013, Mac-Gray sent a letter to BofA Merrill Lynch terminating their engagement in connection with the 2011-2012 Discussions\",\n\"5\":\"Mac-Gray and Moab engaged in a proxy contest leading up to the annual meeting and Mr. Rothenberg and Mr. Hyman were elected in place of Mac-Gray's incumbent nominees\",\n\"6\":\"On May 31, 2013, Mac-Gray entered into an engagement letter with BofA Merrill Lynch with respect to the Board's undertaking a review of strategic alternatives, including a potential sale process\",\n\"7\":\"Party A submitted an unsolicited proposal to the Mac-Gray Board of Directors offering to purchase Mac-Gray for an all-cash purchase price of $17.00 to $19.00 per share\",\n\"8\":\"it would be in the best interests of stockholders to consider a potential sale of Mac-Gray and to review this alternative as compared to Mac-Gray's continuing as a stand-alone company\",\n\"9\":\"50 parties, including CSC and Pamplona, who together we refer to as CSC/Pamplona, and Party A, to solicit potential interest in a transaction with Mac-Gray\",\n\"10\":\"in accordance with the directives of the Special Committee, BofA Merrill Lynch contacted the strategic and financial parties identified at the June 24th Special Committee meeting\",\n\"11\":\"15 of which were potential strategic buyers and 35 of which were potential financial buyers\",\n\"12\":\"Later on June 28, 2013, Party B, entered into a confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray and was provided with an informational package\",\n\"13\":\"On June 30, 2013, Party C entered into a confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray and was provided with an informational package\",\n\"14\":\"the Special Committee decided to deny the exclusivity request at this stage of the process\",\n\"15\":\"On July 11, 2013, CSC/Pamplona entered into a confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray and were provided with an informational package\",\n\"16\":\"which they were instructed to submit by July 23, 2013\",\n\"17\":\"On July 23, 2013, CSC/Pamplona submitted a preliminary indication of interest at an all-cash purchase price of $18.50 per share\",\n\"18\":\"a total of 20 potential bidders, including two strategic bidders (Party A and CSC/Pamplona) and 18 financial bidders (including Party B and Party C), entered into confidentiality agreements with Mac-Gray\",\n\"19\":\"On July 24, 2013, Party B submitted a preliminary indication of interest at an all-cash purchase price of $17.00 to $18.00 per share\",\n\"20\":\"representatives from Party C called BofA Merrill Lynch and presented an oral preliminary indication of interest at an all-cash purchase price of $15.00 to $17.00 per share\",\n\"21\":\"entered into confidentiality agreements with Mac-Gray on a form provided by Mac-Gray, the terms of which were individually negotiated with potential bidders\",\n\"22\":\"the Special Committee authorized and instructed BofA Merrill Lynch to proceed with the staged disclosure as discussed at this meeting\",\n\"23\":\"Later on July 25, 2013, Party C submitted a written indication of interest at an all-cash purchase price of $16.00 to $16.50 per share\",\n\"24\":\"On August 5, 2013, Party A entered into a confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray and was provided with an informational package\",\n\"25\":\"Party B and Party C, in light of the fact that they were financial bidders, were given broad access to an electronic data site\",\n\"26\":\"sent a letter to each of Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona instructing such bidders to submit revised written proposals no later than September 9, 2013\",\n\"27\":\"instructing such bidders to submit revised written proposals no later than September 9, 2013\",\n\"28\":\"On September 9, 2013, CSC/Pamplona submitted a revised indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $19.50 per share\",\n\"29\":\"On September 9, 2013, Party B also submitted a revised indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $18.50 per share\",\n\"30\":\"On September 10, 2013, Party A submitted a revised indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $18.00 to $19.00 per share\",\n\"31\":\"a representative of Party C indicated that it was submitting a revised oral indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $16.00 to $17.00 per share\",\n\"32\":\"Mr. MacDonald indicated that he had decided that he was not interested in rolling over any of his shares in any transaction\",\n\"33\":\"the Special Committee instructed BofA Merrill Lynch to call each of Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona to request final indications of interest by September 18, 2013\",\n\"34\":\"to request final indications of interest by September 18, 2013\",\n\"35\":\"On September 18, 2013, CSC/Pamplona submitted a proposal for an all-cash purchase price of $20.75 per share\",\n\"36\":\"that its previous indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $18.00 to $19.00 per share was its best and final offer\",\n\"37\":\"Party B also submitted a revised indication of interest with a purchase price that Party B valued at $21.50 per share, including $19.00 of cash to be paid at closing\",\n\"38\":\"Party C did not submit a revised indication of interest or reiterate its prior indication of interest of an all-cash purchase price of $16.00 to $17.00 per share\",\n\"39\":\"the Special Committee authorized the Transaction Committee to inform CSC/Pamplona that the Special Committee would be prepared to move into exclusivity at a price of $21.25 per share\",\n\"40\":\"CSC/Pamplona were willing to increase their all-cash purchase price to $21.25 per share as a last and best offer\",\n\"41\":\"On September 24, 2013, CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray executed the exclusivity agreement providing for exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on October 12, 2013\",\n\"42\":\"the revised indication of interest submitted by CSC/Pamplona had the potential of delivering the most value to stockholders\",\n\"44\":\"Goodwin Procter delivered to Kirkland & Ellis LLP, outside legal counsel to CSC/Pamplona, whom we refer to as Kirkland, the initial draft of the merger agreement\",\n\"45\":\"Mr. Daoust reported to the Special Committee that, after discussions between Moab and representatives of Pamplona, it was determined that Moab would not rollover any Moab shares in the transaction\",\n\"46\":\"On October 12, 2013, CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray executed a letter agreement extending exclusivity until 11:59 p.m. ET on October 15, 2013\",\n\"47\":\"on October 14, 2013, the merger agreement was executed, the Pamplona commitment letter was delivered, Moab and Parent executed the Moab voting agreement and the Mac-Donald voting agreements became effective\",\n\"48\":\"On October 15, 2013, before the U.S. stock markets opened, Mac-Gray and CSC jointly announced the execution of the merger agreement\",\n\"MS\":\"Except for Morgan Stanley & Co. LLC, Deutsche Bank Securities Inc. and Evercore Group L.L.C., there is no investment banker\",\n}\n\nfor k, q in quotes.items():\n    idx, pages = find(q)\n    wc = len(q.split())\n    print(f\"{k:>3} words={wc:2} pages={pages} {'OK' if idx is not None else 'NOT FOUND'}\")\nPYEOF"},"output":"---- now the real approach ----\n  1 words=28 pages=['27'] OK\n  2 words=28 pages=['27'] OK\n  3 words=19 pages=['27'] OK\n  4 words=21 pages=['29'] OK\n  5 words=28 pages=['29'] OK\n  6 words=30 pages=['30'] OK\n  7 words=27 pages=['30'] OK\n  8 words=30 pages=['31'] OK\n  9 words=25 pages=['32'] OK\n 10 words=26 pages=['32'] OK\n 11 words=15 pages=['32'] OK\n 12 words=23 pages=['32'] OK\n 13 words=22 pages=['32'] OK\n 14 words=15 pages=['33'] OK\n 15 words=21 pages=['33'] OK\n 16 words=10 pages=['32'] OK\n 17 words=20 pages=['33'] OK\n 18 words=30 pages=['32'] OK\n 19 words=23 pages=['33'] OK\n 20 words=27 pages=['33'] OK\n 21 words=22 pages=['32'] OK\n 22 words=20 pages=['34'] OK\n 23 words=24 pages=['34'] OK\n 24 words=22 pages=['34'] OK\n 25 words=24 pages=['34'] OK\n 26 words=28 pages=['35'] OK\n 27 words=14 pages=['35'] OK\n 28 words=20 pages=['35'] OK\n 29 words=22 pages=['35'] OK\n 30 words=23 pages=['35'] OK\n 31 words=27 pages=['35'] OK\n 32 words=22 pages=['35'] OK\n 33 words=29 pages=['36'] OK\n 34 words=10 pages=['36'] OK\n 35 words=17 pages=['36'] OK\n 36 words=23 pages=['36'] OK\n 37 words=30 pages=['36'] OK\n 38 words=28 pages=['36'] OK\n 39 words=28 pages=[] NOT FOUND\n 40 words=19 pages=['37'] OK\n 41 words=24 pages=['38'] OK\n 42 words=