{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789825495026,"sessionID":"ses_f461fa331ffe0Vx8rAYcMiXg6i","part":{"partID":"prt_0b9e9ad2b001cs65T4cBBg2uoK","sessionID":"ses_f461fa331ffe0Vx8rAYcMiXg6i","messageID":"msg_0b9e98133001kgRbkNUSAw4Erv","type":"tool","id":"call_00_jEGRzH6al9w0migR8Iz21198","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/opencode/work && python3 - <<'PYEOF'\nfrom openpyxl import load_workbook\nwb = load_workbook('/home/uctpiaj/work/extraction/mac-gray.xlsx')\nprint(\"sheets:\", wb.sheetnames)\nfor name in wb.sheetnames:\n    ws = wb[name]\n    print(f\"\\n=== {name}: dims={ws.dimensions}, freeze={ws.freeze_panes}, filter={ws.auto_filter.ref}, merged={list(ws.merged_cells.ranges)}\")\nws = wb['Deal ledger']\nfor row in ws.iter_rows(min_row=1, max_row=ws.max_row, values_only=True):\n    print(\" | \".join(\"\" if v is None else str(v) for v in row[:18]))\nPYEOF"},"output":"sheets: ['Deal ledger', 'Rounds', 'Questions', 'Deal facts']\n\n=== Deal ledger: dims=A1:V52, freeze=A2, filter=A1:V52, merged=[]\n\n=== Rounds: dims=A1:J5, freeze=A2, filter=A1:J5, merged=[]\n\n=== Questions: dims=A1:G5, freeze=A2, filter=A1:G5, merged=[]\n\n=== Deal facts: dims=A1:B17, freeze=A2, filter=A1:B17, merged=[]\n# | When | Who | Type | Event | Process | Round | Price low | Price high | All cash | Formality | Conditions | Count | Exit reason | Inferred | Note | Quote and page | Flag\n1 | 10/23/2012 | BofA Merrill Lynch |  | Adviser | 1 | 0 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Engaged by Mac-Gray for the 2011-2012 Discussions on a possible Mac-Gray acquisition of CSC (not a sale of Mac-Gray); mandate terminated 05/15/2013 and replaced by the 2013 sale-process engagement. | “In connection with Mac-Gray's consideration of a possible acquisition of CSC, which we refer to as the 2011-2012 Discussions, Mac-Gray engaged BofA Merrill Lynch on October 23, 2012” (p. 27) | \n2 | 04/08/2013 | Party A | Strategic | Target interest | 1 | 0 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Following the April 5 Board authorization to explore transactional opportunities with BofA, BofA telephoned Party A, which indicated it might consider a business combination; no price discussed. | “representatives of BofA Merrill Lynch, as instructed by the Board, telephoned a representative of Party A to discuss generally a possible business combination between Party A and Mac-Gray” (p. 27) | \n3 | 05/09/2013 | Goodwin Procter LLP |  | Adviser | 1 | 0 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Outside legal counsel to Mac-Gray; first seen acting at the May 9, 2013 Board meeting; advised the Transaction and Special Committees through signing. | “Goodwin Procter LLP, outside legal counsel to Mac-Gray, were also in attendance for all or portions of the meeting” (p. 27) | \n4 | 05/15/2013 | BofA Merrill Lynch |  | Adviser ended | 1 | 0 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Transaction Committee decided 05/14/2013 to terminate BofA's 2011-2012 engagement letter, given CSC's sale process had ended and BofA was a candidate for the new mandate; termination letter sent 05/15/2013. | “On May 15, 2013, Mac-Gray sent a letter to BofA Merrill Lynch terminating their engagement in connection with the 2011-2012 Discussions” (p. 29) | \n5 | 05/30/2013 | Moab Partners, L.P. (Moab) |  | Activist | 1 | 0 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Proxy contest leading up to the annual meeting; Moab's nominees Michael Rothenberg and James Hyman elected in place of two incumbents; Rothenberg later excluded from sale-process deliberations over a possible Moab rollover. | “Mac-Gray and Moab engaged in a proxy contest leading up to the annual meeting and Mr. Rothenberg and Mr. Hyman were elected in place of Mac-Gray's incumbent nominees” (p. 29) | \n6 | 05/31/2013 | BofA Merrill Lynch |  | Adviser | 1 | 0 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Board approved the engagement 05/30/2013 after three banks presented; BofA agreed not to source acquisition financing for any buyer without Mac-Gray's prior written consent. | “On May 31, 2013, Mac-Gray entered into an engagement letter with BofA Merrill Lynch with respect to the Board's undertaking a review of strategic alternatives, including a potential sale process” (p. 30) | \n7 | 06/21/2013 | Party A | Strategic | Bid | 1 | 0 | 17 | 19 | Yes | Informal | Heavy | 1 |  |  | Unsolicited first proposal, before any NDA or diligence access; all-cash range $17.00-$19.00; Conditions Heavy by context (no substantive diligence access yet). | “Party A submitted an unsolicited proposal to the Mac-Gray Board of Directors offering to purchase Mac-Gray for an all-cash purchase price of $17.00 to $19.00 per share” (p. 30) | \n8 | 06/24/2013 | Mac-Gray (Special Committee) |  | Target sale decision | 1 | 1 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Special Committee of six independent directors formed (Bullock chairman) and concluded it was in stockholders' best interests to consider a potential sale, compared with continuing as a stand-alone company. | “it would be in the best interests of stockholders to consider a potential sale of Mac-Gray and to review this alternative as compared to Mac-Gray's continuing as a stand-alone company” (p. 31) | \n9 | 06/24/2013 | Mac-Gray (Special Committee) |  | Round opened | 1 | 1 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Round 1: approach 50 parties (15 potential strategic, 35 potential financial) to solicit preliminary indications, due 07/23/2013; outreach executed over the following weeks. | “50 parties, including CSC and Pamplona, who together we refer to as CSC/Pamplona, and Party A, to solicit potential interest in a transaction with Mac-Gray” (p. 32) | \n10 | after 06/24/2013 | 15 potential strategic buyers | Strategic | Contact | 1 | 1 |  |  |  |  |  | 15 |  |  | First outreach wave by BofA for Mac-Gray; 15 of the 50 parties approached were potential strategic buyers; contacts continued over the following weeks. | “15 of which were potential strategic buyers and 35 of which were potential financial buyers” (p. 32) | \n11 | after 06/24/2013 | 35 potential financial buyers | Financial | Contact | 1 | 1 |  |  |  |  |  | 35 |  |  | First outreach wave by BofA for Mac-Gray; 35 of the 50 parties were potential financial buyers, including private equity firms. | “in accordance with the directives of the Special Committee, BofA Merrill Lynch contacted the strategic and financial parties identified at the June 24th Special Committee meeting” (p. 32) | \n12 | 06/28/2013 | Party B | Financial | NDA signed | 1 | 1 |  |  |  |  |  | 1 |  |  | Confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray; informational package provided to formulate a preliminary indication of interest. | “Later on June 28, 2013, Party B, entered into a confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray and was provided with an informational package” (p. 32) | \n13 | 06/30/2013 | Party C | Financial | NDA signed | 1 | 1 |  |  |  |  |  | 1 |  |  | Confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray; informational package provided to formulate a preliminary indication of interest. | “On June 30, 2013, Party C entered into a confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray and was provided with an informational package” (p. 32) | \n14 | 07/06/2013 | Moab Partners, L.P. (Moab) |  | Other material event | 1 | 1 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Denied Moab's request to negotiate exclusively with CSC/Pamplona over an equity rollover; Special Committee said it was premature but discussions would be permitted later. | “the Special Committee decided to deny the exclusivity request at this stage of the process” (p. 33) | \n15 | 07/11/2013 | CSC/Pamplona | Strategic | NDA signed | 1 | 1 |  |  |  |  |  | 1 |  |  | Confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray; Pamplona said business and legal diligence would be minimal given its familiarity with Mac-Gray. | “On July 11, 2013, CSC/Pamplona entered into a confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray and were provided with an informational package” (p. 33) | \n16 | 07/23/2013 | Mac-Gray (BofA Merrill Lynch) |  | Deadline | 1 | 1 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Round 1 due date for preliminary indications. CSC/Pamplona bid on time; Party B and Party C indications arrived 07/24 and were considered. | “which they were instructed to submit by July 23, 2013” (p. 32) | Q2\n17 | 07/23/2013 | CSC/Pamplona | Strategic | Bid | 1 | 1 | 18.5 | 18.5 | Yes | Informal | Heavy | 1 |  |  | Preliminary indication of interest submitted on the 07/23 due date; no financing disclosure and no substantive diligence access yet, so Heavy by context. | “On July 23, 2013, CSC/Pamplona submitted a preliminary indication of interest at an all-cash purchase price of $18.50 per share” (p. 33) | \n18 | by 07/23/2013 | 16 financial NDA signers (residual) | Financial | Did not submit | 1 | 1 |  |  |  |  |  | 16 | Not stated | Y | Arithmetic: 20 signers less Party A (not yet signed) and the three submitters (CSC/Pamplona, Party B, Party C) leaves 16 financial signers with no indication by the 07/23 due date. | “a total of 20 potential bidders, including two strategic bidders (Party A and CSC/Pamplona) and 18 financial bidders (including Party B and Party C), entered into confidentiality agreements with Mac-Gray” (p. 32) | Q4\n19 | 07/24/2013 | Party B | Financial | Bid | 1 | 1 | 17 | 18 | Yes | Informal | Heavy | 1 |  |  | Preliminary indication one day after the 07/23 due date, accepted and reviewed at the 07/25 meeting; no substantive diligence access yet. | “On July 24, 2013, Party B submitted a preliminary indication of interest at an all-cash purchase price of $17.00 to $18.00 per share” (p. 33) | \n20 | 07/24/2013 | Party C | Financial | Bid | 1 | 1 | 15 | 17 | Yes | Informal | Heavy | 1 |  |  | Oral indication by telephone, one day after the due date; superseded by the written indication at #23; no substantive diligence access yet. | “representatives from Party C called BofA Merrill Lynch and presented an oral preliminary indication of interest at an all-cash purchase price of $15.00 to $17.00 per share” (p. 33) | \n21 | 06/24/2013-08/24/2013 (over the next two months) | 16 financial NDA signers (residual) | Financial | NDA signed | 1 | 1 |  |  |  |  |  | 16 |  |  | Residual of 18 financial confidentiality signers after Party B and Party C; 20 total signers including Party A and CSC/Pamplona, who have their own rows; signed over two months. | “entered into confidentiality agreements with Mac-Gray on a form provided by Mac-Gray, the terms of which were individually negotiated with potential bidders” (p. 32) | Q4\n22 | 07/25/2013 | Mac-Gray (Special Committee) |  | Round opened | 1 | 2 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Round 2: four bidders advanced to staged disclosure, management presentations and electronic data-site access; revised indications to follow, letters sent 08/27. | “the Special Committee authorized and instructed BofA Merrill Lynch to proceed with the staged disclosure as discussed at this meeting” (p. 34) | \n23 | 07/25/2013 | Party C | Financial | Bid | 1 | 1 | 16 | 16.5 | Yes | Informal | Heavy | 1 |  |  | Written indication submitted later the same day, a late response to round 1 (nothing was due that day); revises #20; financing not addressed. | “Later on July 25, 2013, Party C submitted a written indication of interest at an all-cash purchase price of $16.00 to $16.50 per share” (p. 34) | \n24 | 08/05/2013 | Party A | Strategic | NDA signed | 1 | 2 |  |  |  |  |  | 1 |  |  | Signed after non-solicitation terms were agreed 07/27; informational package provided so Party A could improve the terms of its 06/21 proposal. | “On August 5, 2013, Party A entered into a confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray and was provided with an informational package” (p. 34) | \n25 | between 08/06/2013 and 08/27/2013 | Party A and CSC/Pamplona; Party B and Party C |  | Other material event | 1 | 2 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Access difference: Party B and Party C (financial) received broad data-site access; Party A and CSC/Pamplona (strategic) received limited access, with customer data and locations reserved. | “Party B and Party C, in light of the fact that they were financial bidders, were given broad access to an electronic data site” (p. 34) | \n26 | 08/27/2013 | Mac-Gray (BofA Merrill Lynch) |  | Deadline set | 1 | 2 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | BofA sent letters to all four bidders, once their diligence was substantially complete, requesting revised written proposals by 09/09/2013. | “sent a letter to each of Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona instructing such bidders to submit revised written proposals no later than September 9, 2013” (p. 35) | \n27 | 09/09/2013 | Mac-Gray (BofA Merrill Lynch) |  | Deadline | 1 | 2 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Round 2 due date. CSC/Pamplona and Party B submitted on time; Party A and Party C submitted 09/10 and were considered. | “instructing such bidders to submit revised written proposals no later than September 9, 2013” (p. 35) | Q2\n28 | 09/09/2013 | CSC/Pamplona | Strategic | Bid | 1 | 2 | 19.5 | 19.5 | Yes | Informal | Light | 1 |  |  | Revised indication; Pamplona committed to provide 100% of capital; requested two weeks of exclusive negotiations; submitted on the due date. | “On September 9, 2013, CSC/Pamplona submitted a revised indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $19.50 per share” (p. 35) | \n29 | 09/09/2013 | Party B | Financial | Bid | 1 | 2 | 18.5 | 18.5 | Yes | Informal | Heavy | 1 |  |  | Revised indication; equity from affiliated funds plus third-party debt; no firm financing commitment reported; submitted on the due date. | “On September 9, 2013, Party B also submitted a revised indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $18.50 per share” (p. 35) | \n30 | 09/10/2013 | Party A | Strategic | Bid | 1 | 2 | 18 | 19 | Yes | Informal | Heavy | 1 |  |  | First submission under its NDA, one day after the due date; to be financed by outstanding credit facilities or affiliated equity sources; no firm financing commitment. | “On September 10, 2013, Party A submitted a revised indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $18.00 to $19.00 per share” (p. 35) | \n31 | 09/10/2013 | Party C | Financial | Bid | 1 | 2 | 16 | 17 | Yes | Informal | Heavy | 1 |  |  | Revised oral indication, one day after the due date; no firm financing commitment; Party C's last priced bid. | “a representative of Party C indicated that it was submitting a revised oral indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $16.00 to $17.00 per share” (p. 35) | \n32 | 09/11/2013 | Stewart G. MacDonald, Jr. (CEO and stockholder) |  | Other material event | 1 | 2 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Declined to roll over any shares after being briefed; the committee then agreed to brief him fully (09/12); his support was seen as critical, and he later backed $21.25. | “Mr. MacDonald indicated that he had decided that he was not interested in rolling over any of his shares in any transaction” (p. 35) | \n33 | 09/11/2013 | Mac-Gray (Special Committee) |  | Round opened | 1 | 3 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Round 3: final indications requested from all four bidders by 09/18/2013; bidders told Mac-Gray would consider a short period of exclusive negotiation with one bidder. | “the Special Committee instructed BofA Merrill Lynch to call each of Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona to request final indications of interest by September 18, 2013” (p. 36) | \n34 | 09/18/2013 | Mac-Gray (BofA Merrill Lynch) |  | Deadline | 1 | 3 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Round 3 (final) due date. CSC/Pamplona, Party A and Party B responded; Party C made no submission; the Special Committee met 09/19 on the bids in hand. | “to request final indications of interest by September 18, 2013” (p. 36) | Q2\n35 | 09/18/2013 | CSC/Pamplona | Strategic | Bid | 1 | 3 | 20.75 | 20.75 | Yes | Formal | Light | 1 |  |  | Final indication responding to the 09/18 final request; Pamplona reiterated its 100% capital commitment; requested two weeks of exclusive negotiations. | “On September 18, 2013, CSC/Pamplona submitted a proposal for an all-cash purchase price of $20.75 per share” (p. 36) | \n36 | 09/18/2013 | Party A | Strategic | Bid reaffirmed | 1 | 3 | 18 | 19 | Yes | Formal | Heavy | 1 |  |  | Reaffirmed by telephone that the standing $18.00-$19.00 indication (carried from #30) was its best and final offer; financing still not committed. | “that its previous indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $18.00 to $19.00 per share was its best and final offer” (p. 36) | \n37 | 09/18/2013 | Party B | Financial | Bid | 1 | 3 | 21.5 | 21.5 | No | Formal | Heavy | 1 |  |  | Package valued at $21.50 per share: $19.00 cash at closing plus options valued at $2.50 (10% of new equity, vesting on base-case projections over five years); no firm financing commitment. | “Party B also submitted a revised indication of interest with a purchase price that Party B valued at $21.50 per share, including $19.00 of cash to be paid at closing” (p. 36) | \n38 | 09/18/2013 | Party C | Financial | Did not submit | 1 | 3 |  |  |  |  |  | 1 | Not stated |  | No submission in the final round and did not reiterate its $16.00-$17.00 indication; the filing gives no reasons. | “Party C did not submit a revised indication of interest or reiterate its prior indication of interest of an all-cash purchase price of $16.00 to $17.00 per share” (p. 36) | \n39 | 09/19/2013 | Mac-Gray (Special Committee) |  | Round opened | 1 | 4 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Round 4: Special Committee selected CSC/Pamplona as most valuable and authorized exclusivity at $21.25 per share; Mr. MacDonald indicated support at that price. | “The Special Committee then authorized the Transaction Committee to inform CSC/Pamplona that the Special Committee would be prepared to move into exclusivity at a price of $21.25 per share” (p. 37) | Q1\n40 | 09/21/2013 | CSC/Pamplona | Strategic | Bid | 1 | 4 | 21.25 | 21.25 | Yes | Formal | Light | 1 |  |  | Last and best offer at the $21.25 price the Special Committee required, conditioned on a two-week exclusive negotiation; requested MacDonald voting agreements. | “CSC/Pamplona were willing to increase their all-cash purchase price to $21.25 per share as a last and best offer” (p. 37) | Q1\n41 | 09/24/2013 | CSC/Pamplona and Mac-Gray |  | Exclusivity changed | 1 | 4 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Executed with CSC/Pamplona until 5 p.m. ET 10/12/2013; included a $15 million reverse termination fee, no financing contingency and Pamplona funding of 100% of capital; auto-termination on adverse change. | “On September 24, 2013, CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray executed the exclusivity agreement providing for exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on October 12, 2013” (p. 38) | \n42 | 09/24/2013 | Party A | Strategic | Dropped by target | 1 | 3 |  |  |  |  |  | 1 | Not stated | Y | Live rival when Mac-Gray executed exclusivity with CSC/Pamplona; the filing reports no notice to Party A; dropped by the execution. | “the revised indication of interest submitted by CSC/Pamplona had the potential of delivering the most value to stockholders” (p. 37) | Q3\n43 | 09/24/2013 | Party B | Financial | Dropped by target | 1 | 3 |  |  |  |  |  | 1 | Not stated | Y | Live rival when Mac-Gray executed exclusivity with CSC/Pamplona; the filing reports no notice to Party B; dropped by the execution. | “On September 24, 2013, CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray executed the exclusivity agreement providing for exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on October 12, 2013” (p. 38) | Q3\n44 | 09/25/2013 | Kirkland & Ellis LLP |  | Adviser | 1 | 4 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Outside legal counsel to CSC/Pamplona; first seen acting when Goodwin Procter delivered the initial draft merger agreement; represented CSC/Pamplona through signing. | “Goodwin Procter delivered to Kirkland & Ellis LLP, outside legal counsel to CSC/Pamplona, whom we refer to as Kirkland, the initial draft of the merger agreement” (p. 38) | \n45 | 10/07/2013 | Moab Partners, L.P. (Moab) |  | Other material event | 1 | 4 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | No rollover: after Moab was allowed to resume discussions with Pamplona (09/23), it was determined Moab would not roll over any shares in the transaction. | “Mr. Daoust reported to the Special Committee that, after discussions between Moab and representatives of Pamplona, it was determined that Moab would not rollover any Moab shares in the transaction” (p. 39) | \n46 | 10/12/2013 | CSC/Pamplona and Mac-Gray |  | Exclusivity changed | 1 | 4 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Extended, after CSC/Pamplona requested more time and agreed to an $11 million Mac-Gray termination fee, from 5 p.m. 10/12 to 11:59 p.m. ET 10/15/2013. | “On October 12, 2013, CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray executed a letter agreement extending exclusivity until 11:59 p.m. ET on October 15, 2013” (p. 41) | \n47 | 10/14/2013 | Morgan Stanley & Co. LLC |  | Adviser | 1 | 4 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Financial adviser to Parent (buyer side); first seen in the executed merger agreement; engagement date and role not disclosed. | “Except for Morgan Stanley & Co. LLC, Deutsche Bank Securities Inc. and Evercore Group L.L.C., there is no investment banker” (p. A-30) | \n48 | 10/14/2013 | Deutsche Bank Securities Inc. |  | Adviser | 1 | 4 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Financial adviser to Parent (buyer side); first seen in the executed merger agreement; engagement date and role not disclosed. | “Except for Morgan Stanley & Co. LLC, Deutsche Bank Securities Inc. and Evercore Group L.L.C., there is no investment banker” (p. A-30) | \n49 | 10/14/2013 | Evercore Group L.L.C. |  | Adviser | 1 | 4 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Financial adviser to Parent (buyer side); first seen in the executed merger agreement; engagement date and role not disclosed. | “Except for Morgan Stanley & Co. LLC, Deutsche Bank Securities Inc. and Evercore Group L.L.C., there is no investment banker” (p. A-30) | \n50 | 10/14/2013 | Mac-Gray and CSC/Pamplona |  | Merger agreement signed | 1 | post |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Agreed price $21.25 per share in cash; no financing contingency; Pamplona commitment letter ($594 million) delivered; Moab and MacDonald voting agreements effective. | “on October 14, 2013, the merger agreement was executed, the Pamplona commitment letter was delivered, Moab and Parent executed the Moab voting agreement and the Mac-Donald voting agreements became effective” (p. 41) | \n51 | 10/15/2013 | Mac-Gray and CSC |  | Merger announced | 1 | post |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Joint announcement of the executed merger agreement before the U.S. stock markets opened. | “On October 15, 2013, before the U.S. stock markets opened, Mac-Gray and CSC jointly announced the execution of the merger agreement” (p. 41) | \n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"sheets: ['Deal ledger', 'Rounds', 'Questions', 'Deal facts']\n\n=== Deal ledger: dims=A1:V52, freeze=A2, filter=A1:V52, merged=[]\n\n=== Rounds: dims=A1:J5, freeze=A2, filter=A1:J5, merged=[]\n\n=== Questions: dims=A1:G5, freeze=A2, filter=A1:G5, merged=[]\n\n=== Deal facts: dims=A1:B17, freeze=A2, filter=A1:B17, merged=[]\n# | When | Who | Type | Event | Process | Round | Price low | Price high | All cash | Formality | Conditions | Count | Exit reason | Inferred | Note | Quote and page | Flag\n1 | 10/23/2012 | BofA Merrill Lynch |  | Adviser | 1 | 0 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Engaged by Mac-Gray for the 2011-2012 Discussions on a possible Mac-Gray acquisition of CSC (not a sale of Mac-Gray); mandate terminated 05/15/2013 and replaced by the 2013 sale-process engagement. | “In connection with Mac-Gray's consideration of a possible acquisition of CSC, which we refer to as the 2011-2012 Discussions, Mac-Gray engaged BofA Merrill Lynch on October 23, 2012” (p. 27) | \n2 | 04/08/2013 | Party A | Strategic | Target interest | 1 | 0 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Following the April 5 Board authorization to explore transactional opportunities with BofA, BofA telephoned Party A, which indicated it might consider a business combination; no price discussed. | “representatives of BofA Merrill Lynch, as instructed by the Board, telephoned a representative of Party A to discuss generally a possible business combination between Party A and Mac-Gray” (p. 27) | \n3 | 05/09/2013 | Goodwin Procter LLP |  | Adviser | 1 | 0 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Outside legal counsel to Mac-Gray; first seen acting at the May 9, 2013 Board meeting; advised the Transaction and Special Committees through signing. | “Goodwin Procter LLP, outside legal counsel to Mac-Gray, were also in attendance for all or portions of the meeting” (p. 27) | \n4 | 05/15/2013 | BofA Merrill Lynch |  | Adviser ended | 1 | 0 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Transaction Committee decided 05/14/2013 to terminate BofA's 2011-2012 engagement letter, given CSC's sale process had ended and BofA was a candidate for the new mandate; termination letter sent 05/15/2013. | “On May 15, 2013, Mac-Gray sent a letter to BofA Merrill Lynch terminating their engagement in connection with the 2011-2012 Discussions” (p. 29) | \n5 | 05/30/2013 | Moab Partners, L.P. (Moab) |  | Activist | 1 | 0 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Proxy contest leading up to the annual meeting; Moab's nominees Michael Rothenberg and James Hyman elected in place of two incumbents; Rothenberg later excluded from sale-process deliberations over a possible Moab rollover. | “Mac-Gray and Moab engaged in a proxy contest leading up to the annual meeting and Mr. Rothenberg and Mr. Hyman were elected in place of Mac-Gray's incumbent nominees” (p. 29) | \n6 | 05/31/2013 | BofA Merrill Lynch |  | Adviser | 1 | 0 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Board approved the engagement 05/30/2013 after three banks presented; BofA agreed not to source acquisition financing for any buyer without Mac-Gray's prior written consent. | “On May 31, 2013, Mac-Gray entered into an engagement letter with BofA Merrill Lynch with respect to the Board's undertaking a review of strategic alternatives, including a potential sale process” (p. 30) | \n7 | 06/21/2013 | Party A | Strategic | Bid | 1 | 0 | 17 | 19 | Yes | Informal | Heavy | 1 |  |  | Unsolicited first proposal, before any NDA or diligence access; all-cash range $17.00-$19.00; Conditions Heavy by context (no substantive diligence access yet). | “Party A submitted an unsolicited proposal to the Mac-Gray Board of Directors offering to purchase Mac-Gray for an all-cash purchase price of $17.00 to $19.00 per share” (p. 30) | \n8 | 06/24/2013 | Mac-Gray (Special Committee) |  | Target sale decision | 1 | 1 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Special Committee of six independent directors formed (Bullock chairman) and concluded it was in stockholders' best interests to consider a potential sale, compared with continuing as a stand-alone company. | “it would be in the best interests of stockholders to consider a potential sale of Mac-Gray and to review this alternative as compared to Mac-Gray's continuing as a stand-alone company” (p. 31) | \n9 | 06/24/2013 | Mac-Gray (Special Committee) |  | Round opened | 1 | 1 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Round 1: approach 50 parties (15 potential strategic, 35 potential financial) to solicit preliminary indications, due 07/23/2013; outreach executed over the following weeks. | “50 parties, including CSC and Pamplona, who together we refer to as CSC/Pamplona, and Party A, to solicit potential interest in a transaction with Mac-Gray” (p. 32) | \n10 | after 06/24/2013 | 15 potential strategic buyers | Strategic | Contact | 1 | 1 |  |  |  |  |  | 15 |  |  | First outreach wave by BofA for Mac-Gray; 15 of the 50 parties approached were potential strategic buyers; contacts continued over the following weeks. | “15 of which were potential strategic buyers and 35 of which were potential financial buyers” (p. 32) | \n11 | after 06/24/2013 | 35 potential financial buyers | Financial | Contact | 1 | 1 |  |  |  |  |  | 35 |  |  | First outreach wave by BofA for Mac-Gray; 35 of the 50 parties were potential financial buyers, including private equity firms. | “in accordance with the directives of the Special Committee, BofA Merrill Lynch contacted the strategic and financial parties identified at the June 24th Special Committee meeting” (p. 32) | \n12 | 06/28/2013 | Party B | Financial | NDA signed | 1 | 1 |  |  |  |  |  | 1 |  |  | Confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray; informational package provided to formulate a preliminary indication of interest. | “Later on June 28, 2013, Party B, entered into a confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray and was provided with an informational package” (p. 32) | \n13 | 06/30/2013 | Party C | Financial | NDA signed | 1 | 1 |  |  |  |  |  | 1 |  |  | Confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray; informational package provided to formulate a preliminary indication of interest. | “On June 30, 2013, Party C entered into a confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray and was provided with an informational package” (p. 32) | \n14 | 07/06/2013 | Moab Partners, L.P. (Moab) |  | Other material event | 1 | 1 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Denied Moab's request to negotiate exclusively with CSC/Pamplona over an equity rollover; Special Committee said it was premature but discussions would be permitted later. | “the Special Committee decided to deny the exclusivity request at this stage of the process” (p. 33) | \n15 | 07/11/2013 | CSC/Pamplona | Strategic | NDA signed | 1 | 1 |  |  |  |  |  | 1 |  |  | Confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray; Pamplona said business and legal diligence would be minimal given its familiarity with Mac-Gray. | “On July 11, 2013, CSC/Pamplona entered into a confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray and were provided with an informational package” (p. 33) | \n16 | 07/23/2013 | Mac-Gray (BofA Merrill Lynch) |  | Deadline | 1 | 1 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Round 1 due date for preliminary indications. CSC/Pamplona bid on time; Party B and Party C indications arrived 07/24 and were considered. | “which they were instructed to submit by July 23, 2013” (p. 32) | Q2\n17 | 07/23/2013 | CSC/Pamplona | Strategic | Bid | 1 | 1 | 18.5 | 18.5 | Yes | Informal | Heavy | 1 |  |  | Preliminary indication of interest submitted on the 07/23 due date; no financing disclosure and no substantive diligence access yet, so Heavy by context. | “On July 23, 2013, CSC/Pamplona submitted a preliminary indication of interest at an all-cash purchase price of $18.50 per share” (p. 33) | \n18 | by 07/23/2013 | 16 financial NDA signers (residual) | Financial | Did not submit | 1 | 1 |  |  |  |  |  | 16 | Not stated | Y | Arithmetic: 20 signers less Party A (not yet signed) and the three submitters (CSC/Pamplona, Party B, Party C) leaves 16 financial signers with no indication by the 07/23 due date. | “a total of 20 potential bidders, including two strategic bidders (Party A and CSC/Pamplona) and 18 financial bidders (including Party B and Party C), entered into confidentiality agreements with Mac-Gray” (p. 32) | Q4\n19 | 07/24/2013 | Party B | Financial | Bid | 1 | 1 | 17 | 18 | Yes | Informal | Heavy | 1 |  |  | Preliminary indication one day after the 07/23 due date, accepted and reviewed at the 07/25 meeting; no substantive diligence access yet. | “On July 24, 2013, Party B submitted a preliminary indication of interest at an all-cash purchase price of $17.00 to $18.00 per share” (p. 33) | \n20 | 07/24/2013 | Party C | Financial | Bid | 1 | 1 | 15 | 17 | Yes | Informal | Heavy | 1 |  |  | Oral indication by telephone, one day after the due date; superseded by the written indication at #23; no substantive diligence access yet. | “representatives from Party C called BofA Merrill Lynch and presented an oral preliminary indication of interest at an all-cash purchase price of $15.00 to $17.00 per share” (p. 33) | \n21 | 06/24/2013-08/24/2013 (over the next two months) | 16 financial NDA signers (residual) | Financial | NDA signed | 1 | 1 |  |  |  |  |  | 16 |  |  | Residual of 18 financial confidentiality signers after Party B and Party C; 20 total signers including Party A and CSC/Pamplona, who have their own rows; signed over two months. | “entered into confidentiality agreements with Mac-Gray on a form provided by Mac-Gray, the terms of which were individually negotiated with potential bidders” (p. 32) | Q4\n22 | 07/25/2013 | Mac-Gray (Special Committee) |  | Round opened | 1 | 2 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Round 2: four bidders advanced to staged disclosure, management presentations and electronic data-site access; revised indications to follow, letters sent 08/27. | “the Special Committee authorized and instructed BofA Merrill Lynch to proceed with the staged disclosure as discussed at this meeting” (p. 34) | \n23 | 07/25/2013 | Party C | Financial | Bid | 1 | 1 | 16 | 16.5 | Yes | Informal | Heavy | 1 |  |  | Written indication submitted later the same day, a late response to round 1 (nothing was due that day); revises #20; financing not addressed. | “Later on July 25, 2013, Party C submitted a written indication of interest at an all-cash purchase price of $16.00 to $16.50 per share” (p. 34) | \n24 | 08/05/2013 | Party A | Strategic | NDA signed | 1 | 2 |  |  |  |  |  | 1 |  |  | Signed after non-solicitation terms were agreed 07/27; informational package provided so Party A could improve the terms of its 06/21 proposal. | “On August 5, 2013, Party A entered into a confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray and was provided with an informational package” (p. 34) | \n25 | between 08/06/2013 and 08/27/2013 | Party A and CSC/Pamplona; Party B and Party C |  | Other material event | 1 | 2 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Access difference: Party B and Party C (financial) received broad data-site access; Party A and CSC/Pamplona (strategic) received limited access, with customer data and locations reserved. | “Party B and Party C, in light of the fact that they were financial bidders, were given broad access to an electronic data site” (p. 34) | \n26 | 08/27/2013 | Mac-Gray (BofA Merrill Lynch) |  | Deadline set | 1 | 2 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | BofA sent letters to all four bidders, once their diligence was substantially complete, requesting revised written proposals by 09/09/2013. | “sent a letter to each of Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona instructing such bidders to submit revised written proposals no later than September 9, 2013” (p. 35) | \n27 | 09/09/2013 | Mac-Gray (BofA Merrill Lynch) |  | Deadline | 1 | 2 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Round 2 due date. CSC/Pamplona and Party B submitted on time; Party A and Party C submitted 09/10 and were considered. | “instructing such bidders to submit revised written proposals no later than September 9, 2013” (p. 35) | Q2\n28 | 09/09/2013 | CSC/Pamplona | Strategic | Bid | 1 | 2 | 19.5 | 19.5 | Yes | Informal | Light | 1 |  |  | Revised indication; Pamplona committed to provide 100% of capital; requested two weeks of exclusive negotiations; submitted on the due date. | “On September 9, 2013, CSC/Pamplona submitted a revised indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $19.50 per share” (p. 35) | \n29 | 09/09/2013 | Party B | Financial | Bid | 1 | 2 | 18.5 | 18.5 | Yes | Informal | Heavy | 1 |  |  | Revised indication; equity from affiliated funds plus third-party debt; no firm financing commitment reported; submitted on the due date. | “On September 9, 2013, Party B also submitted a revised indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $18.50 per share” (p. 35) | \n30 | 09/10/2013 | Party A | Strategic | Bid | 1 | 2 | 18 | 19 | Yes | Informal | Heavy | 1 |  |  | First submission under its NDA, one day after the due date; to be financed by outstanding credit facilities or affiliated equity sources; no firm financing commitment. | “On September 10, 2013, Party A submitted a revised indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $18.00 to $19.00 per share” (p. 35) | \n31 | 09/10/2013 | Party C | Financial | Bid | 1 | 2 | 16 | 17 | Yes | Informal | Heavy | 1 |  |  | Revised oral indication, one day after the due date; no firm financing commitment; Party C's last priced bid. | “a representative of Party C indicated that it was submitting a revised oral indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $16.00 to $17.00 per share” (p. 35) | \n32 | 09/11/2013 | Stewart G. MacDonald, Jr. (CEO and stockholder) |  | Other material event | 1 | 2 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Declined to roll over any shares after being briefed; the committee then agreed to brief him fully (09/12); his support was seen as critical, and he later backed $21.25. | “Mr. MacDonald indicated that he had decided that he was not interested in rolling over any of his shares in any transaction” (p. 35) | \n33 | 09/11/2013 | Mac-Gray (Special Committee) |  | Round opened | 1 | 3 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Round 3: final indications requested from all four bidders by 09/18/2013; bidders told Mac-Gray would consider a short period of exclusive negotiation with one bidder. | “the Special Committee instructed BofA Merrill Lynch to call each of Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona to request final indications of interest by September 18, 2013” (p. 36) | \n34 | 09/18/2013 | Mac-Gray (BofA Merrill Lynch) |  | Deadline | 1 | 3 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Round 3 (final) due date. CSC/Pamplona, Party A and Party B responded; Party C made no submission; the Special Committee met 09/19 on the bids in hand. | “to request final indications of interest by September 18, 2013” (p. 36) | Q2\n35 | 09/18/2013 | CSC/Pamplona | Strategic | Bid | 1 | 3 | 20.75 | 20.75 | Yes | Formal | Light | 1 |  |  | Final indication responding to the 09/18 final request; Pamplona reiterated its 100% capital commitment; requested two weeks of exclusive negotiations. | “On September 18, 2013, CSC/Pamplona submitted a proposal for an all-cash purchase price of $20.75 per share” (p. 36) | \n36 | 09/18/2013 | Party A | Strategic | Bid reaffirmed | 1 | 3 | 18 | 19 | Yes | Formal | Heavy | 1 |  |  | Reaffirmed by telephone that the standing $18.00-$19.00 indication (carried from #30) was its best and final offer; financing still not committed. | “that its previous indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $18.00 to $19.00 per share was its best and final offer” (p. 36) | \n37 | 09/18/2013 | Party B | Financial | Bid | 1 | 3 | 21.5 | 21.5 | No | Formal | Heavy | 1 |  |  | Package valued at $21.50 per share: $19.00 cash at closing plus options valued at $2.50 (10% of new equity, vesting on base-case projections over five years); no firm financing commitment. | “Party B also submitted a revised indication of interest with a purchase price that Party B valued at $21.50 per share, including $19.00 of cash to be paid at closing” (p. 36) | \n38 | 09/18/2013 | Party C | Financial | Did not submit | 1 | 3 |  |  |  |  |  | 1 | Not stated |  | No submission in the final round and did not reiterate its $16.00-$17.00 indication; the filing gives no reasons. | “Party C did not submit a revised indication of interest or reiterate its prior indication of interest of an all-cash purchase price of $16.00 to $17.00 per share” (p. 36) | \n39 | 09/19/2013 | Mac-Gray (Special Committee) |  | Round opened | 1 | 4 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Round 4: Special Committee selected CSC/Pamplona as most valuable and authorized exclusivity at $21.25 per share; Mr. MacDonald indicated support at that price. | “The Special Committee then authorized the Transaction Committee to inform CSC/Pamplona that the Special Committee would be prepared to move into exclusivity at a price of $21.25 per share” (p. 37) | Q1\n40 | 09/21/2013 | CSC/Pamplona | Strategic | Bid | 1 | 4 | 21.25 | 21.25 | Yes | Formal | Light | 1 |  |  | Last and best offer at the $21.25 price the Special Committee required, conditioned on a two-week exclusive negotiation; requested MacDonald voting agreements. | “CSC/Pamplona were willing to increase their all-cash purchase price to $21.25 per share as a last and best offer” (p. 37) | Q1\n41 | 09/24/2013 | CSC/Pamplona and Mac-Gray |  | Exclusivity changed | 1 | 4 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Executed with CSC/Pamplona until 5 p.m. ET 10/12/2013; included a $15 million reverse termination fee, no financing contingency and Pamplona funding of 100% of capital; auto-termination on adverse change. | “On September 24, 2013, CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray executed the exclusivity agreement providing for exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on October 12, 2013” (p. 38) | \n42 | 09/24/2013 | Party A | Strategic | Dropped by target | 1 | 3 |  |  |  |  |  | 1 | Not stated | Y | Live rival when Mac-Gray executed exclusivity with CSC/Pamplona; the filing reports no notice to Party A; dropped by the execution. | “the revised indication of interest submitted by CSC/Pamplona had the potential of delivering the most value to stockholders” (p. 37) | Q3\n43 | 09/24/2013 | Party B | Financial | Dropped by target | 1 | 3 |  |  |  |  |  | 1 | Not stated | Y | Live rival when Mac-Gray executed exclusivity with CSC/Pamplona; the filing reports no notice to Party B; dropped by the execution. | “On September 24, 2013, CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray executed the exclusivity agreement providing for exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on October 12, 2013” (p. 38) | Q3\n44 | 09/25/2013 | Kirkland & Ellis LLP |  | Adviser | 1 | 4 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Outside legal counsel to CSC/Pamplona; first seen acting when Goodwin Procter delivered the initial draft merger agreement; represented CSC/Pamplona through signing. | “Goodwin Procter delivered to Kirkland & Ellis LLP, outside legal counsel to CSC/Pamplona, whom we refer to as Kirkland, the initial draft of the merger agreement” (p. 38) | \n45 | 10/07/2013 | Moab Partners, L.P. (Moab) |  | Other material event | 1 | 4 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | No rollover: after Moab was allowed to resume discussions with Pamplona (09/23), it was determined Moab would not roll over any shares in the transaction. | “Mr. Daoust reported to the Special Committee that, after discussions between Moab and representatives of Pamplona, it was determined that Moab would not rollover any Moab shares in the transaction” (p. 39) | \n46 | 10/12/2013 | CSC/Pamplona and Mac-Gray |  | Exclusivity changed | 1 | 4 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Extended, after CSC/Pamplona requested more time and agreed to an $11 million Mac-Gray termination fee, from 5 p.m. 10/12 to 11:59 p.m. ET 10/15/2013. | “On October 12, 2013, CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray executed a letter agreement extending exclusivity until 11:59 p.m. ET on October 15, 2013” (p. 41) | \n47 | 10/14/2013 | Morgan Stanley & Co. LLC |  | Adviser | 1 | 4 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Financial adviser to Parent (buyer side); first seen in the executed merger agreement; engagement date and role not disclosed. | “Except for Morgan Stanley & Co. LLC, Deutsche Bank Securities Inc. and Evercore Group L.L.C., there is no investment banker” (p. A-30) | \n48 | 10/14/2013 | Deutsche Bank Securities Inc. |  | Adviser | 1 | 4 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Financial adviser to Parent (buyer side); first seen in the executed merger agreement; engagement date and role not disclosed. | “Except for Morgan Stanley & Co. LLC, Deutsche Bank Securities Inc. and Evercore Group L.L.C., there is no investment banker” (p. A-30) | \n49 | 10/14/2013 | Evercore Group L.L.C. |  | Adviser | 1 | 4 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Financial adviser to Parent (buyer side); first seen in the executed merger agreement; engagement date and role not disclosed. | “Except for Morgan Stanley & Co. LLC, Deutsche Bank Securities Inc. and Evercore Group L.L.C., there is no investment banker” (p. A-30) | \n50 | 10/14/2013 | Mac-Gray and CSC/Pamplona |  | Merger agreement signed | 1 | post |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Agreed price $21.25 per share in cash; no financing contingency; Pamplona commitment letter ($594 million) delivered; Moab and MacDonald voting agreements effective. | “on October 14, 2013, the merger agreement was executed, the Pamplona commitment letter was delivered, Moab and Parent executed the Moab voting agreement and the Mac-Donald voting agreements became effective” (p. 41) | \n51 | 10/15/2013 | Mac-Gray and CSC |  | Merger announced | 1 | post |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | Joint announcement of the executed merger agreement before the U.S. stock markets opened. | “On October 15, 2013, before the U.S. stock markets opened, Mac-Gray and CSC jointly announced the execution of the merger agreement” (p. 41) | \n"},{"type":"text","text":"Command exited with code 0."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /tmp/opencode/work && python3 - <<'PYEOF'\\nfrom openpyxl import load_workbook\\nwb = load_workbook('/home/uctpiaj/work/extraction/mac-gray.xlsx')\\nprint(\\\"sheets:\\\", wb.sheetnames)\\nfor name in wb.sheetnames:\\n    ws = wb[name]\\n    print(f\\\"\\\\n=== {name}: dims={ws.dimensions}, freeze={ws.freeze_panes}, filter={ws.auto_filter.ref}, merged={list(ws.merged_cells.ranges)}\\\")\\nws = wb['Deal ledger']\\nfor row in ws.iter_rows(min_row=1, max_row=ws.max_row, values_only=True):\\n    print(\\\" | \\\".join(\\\"\\\" if v is None else str(v) for v in row[:18]))\\nPYEOF\"}"},"time":{"start":1789825494315,"end":1789825495026}}}}
